  "notes": "The Neoclassical façade has an open four-column porch and two open bell chambers. The Gothic nave has flying buttresses, a polygonal apse and transept roses. The connected range retains three open spaces, including the cloister with carved arcade and upper gallery. The mapped cathedral relation defines the complex perimeter and three voids. The historic façade and nave axis use the plaza, map outline and exterior photographs. Roof profiles, tower heights, sculpture, buttresses, cloister tracery and ground levels are exterior reconstructions from photos and standard terrain. The main cloister has an open walk with simplified tracery and stonework. The model covers the connected exterior ensemble. Full church interiors, bells in motion, interior chapels and occupied museum rooms are outside this reconstruction.",
