    "notes": "OSM relation 1727138 identifies the connected cathedral. The Navarrería approach and plaza fix the signed porch orientation. The western steps and walls follow sampled viewer terrain and the three courts stay open. Nearby map features remain independent. The mapped cathedral relation defines the complex perimeter and three voids. The historic façade and nave axis use the plaza, map outline and exterior photographs. Roof profiles, tower heights, sculpture, buttresses, cloister tracery and ground levels are exterior reconstructions from photos and standard terrain. The main cloister has an open walk with simplified tracery and stonework. The model covers the connected exterior ensemble. Full church interiors, bells in motion, interior chapels and occupied museum rooms are outside this reconstruction."
  },
